WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.185
Lesson 1.2.

00:00:02.185 --> 00:00:04.490
How a transaction actually happens.

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:06.455
By the end of this lesson, you'll

00:00:06.455 --> 00:00:08.594
be able to follow a transaction from

00:00:08.594 --> 00:00:11.195
signature to finality, and estimate its cost.

00:00:12.495 --> 00:00:13.785
Here's the plan.

00:00:13.785 --> 00:00:15.470
First, the key ideas.

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:18.185
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:18.185 --> 00:00:19.710
Then, your checklist.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:21.872
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:23.172 --> 00:00:26.867
Lifecycle: create → sign → broadcast → mempool

00:00:26.867 --> 00:00:30.547
(waiting) → included in a block → confirmed

00:00:30.547 --> 00:00:33.427
→ final. Ethereum the price has

00:00:33.427 --> 00:00:36.067
a base fee (burned) plus a

00:00:36.067 --> 00:00:39.155
priority tip (to get included sooner). Gas

00:00:39.155 --> 00:00:41.452
price is quoted in gwei (1 gwei

00:00:41.452 --> 00:00:45.199
= 0.000000001 ETH). low-nonce transaction blocks

00:00:45.199 --> 00:00:48.083
all later ones until it confirms or is

00:00:48.083 --> 00:00:52.449
replaced (same nonce, higher fee). reversed. It differs

00:00:52.449 --> 00:00:53.449
by chain,

00:00:53.449 --> 00:00:55.388
and L2s have their own

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:58.049
rules (Module 5). First, Gas

00:00:58.049 --> 00:01:01.014
is the unit of computation. Cost

00:01:01.014 --> 00:01:03.784
= gas used × gas price.

00:01:03.784 --> 00:01:04.609
On.

00:01:04.609 --> 00:01:08.764
Next, Nonce: each account's transactions are numbered in order.

00:01:08.764 --> 00:01:09.764
A stuck.

00:01:09.764 --> 00:01:12.679
Then, Failed transactions still cost gas.

00:01:12.679 --> 00:01:16.864
The network did the computation even though the result

00:01:16.864 --> 00:01:19.591
was reverted. Also, Finality: the point

00:01:19.591 --> 00:01:22.004
after which a transaction can't

00:01:22.004 --> 00:01:26.365
realistically be. And finally, Explorers (e.g. Etherscan) show status,

00:01:26.365 --> 00:01:29.744
fee, sender, contract called, token transfers and logs.

00:01:31.044 --> 00:01:33.559
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:01:33.559 --> 00:01:39.657
A swap uses 150,000 gas at 20 gwei: 150,000

00:01:39.657 --> 00:01:44.669
× 20 = 3,000,000 gwei = 0.003 ETH.

00:01:44.669 --> 00:01:48.394
At $3,000/ETH that's $9.

00:01:48.394 --> 00:01:51.096
The same swap during congestion

00:01:51.096 --> 00:01:53.169
at 80 gwei costs $36.

00:01:53.169 --> 00:01:56.516
If you're compounding $1.50 of rewards, the

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:59.250
gas costs more than the rewards.

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:01.580
That's why position size matters on-chain.

00:02:02.881 --> 00:02:04.341
Here's your checklist.

00:02:04.341 --> 00:02:05.876
Do it now, for real.

00:02:05.876 --> 00:02:08.781
First, I check the fee estimate before signing.

00:02:08.781 --> 00:02:10.297
Next, I know how to find

00:02:10.297 --> 00:02:12.416
my transaction on an explorer.

00:02:12.416 --> 00:02:15.271
And finally, I know a stuck transaction can be

00:02:15.271 --> 00:02:17.761
sped up or cancelled with the same nonce.

00:02:19.061 --> 00:02:20.271
Question 1.

00:02:20.271 --> 00:02:22.101
Your transaction reverted.

00:02:22.101 --> 00:02:22.916
Did you pay?

00:02:27.336 --> 00:02:29.373
The answer: Yes, for the gas used

00:02:29.373 --> 00:02:30.991
up to the point of failure.

00:02:32.291 --> 00:02:33.536
Question 2.

00:02:33.536 --> 00:02:36.439
200,000 gas at 10 gwei

00:02:36.439 --> 00:02:39.595
with ETH at $2,500 costs?

00:02:44.015 --> 00:02:49.465
The answer: 2,000,000 gwei = 0.002 ETH = $5.

00:02:50.764 --> 00:02:52.034
Question 3.

00:02:52.034 --> 00:02:54.429
Why are your newer transactions all pending?

00:02:58.849 --> 00:03:01.454
The answer: An earlier nonce is stuck.

00:03:01.454 --> 00:03:04.029
Replace or speed it up, and the rest follow.

00:03:05.329 --> 00:03:06.574
Let's recap.

00:03:06.574 --> 00:03:09.585
Gas is the unit of computation: Cost

00:03:09.585 --> 00:03:11.756
= gas used × gas price.

00:03:11.756 --> 00:03:15.451
Nonce: each account's transactions are numbered in order.

00:03:15.451 --> 00:03:17.886
Failed transactions still cost gas.

00:03:17.886 --> 00:03:19.757
Finality: the point after which

00:03:19.757 --> 00:03:21.921
a transaction can't realistically be.

00:03:23.221 --> 00:03:25.736
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:03:25.736 --> 00:03:30.266
Next up, Lesson 1.3: Wallets, keys, hardware & multisig.
